<section class="bhd-page__feature"><div><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Media overview</p><h2>Best Hydrate is an Alberta hydration company building at the intersection of product, science, performance and access</h2><p>The company sells a Canadian consumer hydration powder while developing a broader evidence and partnership platform around oral hydration. Public coverage and interviews should distinguish the current commercial product from research programs, clinical-development work and future humanitarian applications.</p><p>The public site has been rebuilt specifically to make those boundaries easier to verify.</p></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Fast fact paths</p><h2>Go to the source that matches the question</h2><div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4"><article><h3>Company</h3><p>Origin, team, mission and public corporate information.</p><a href="/pages/our-story">Meet Us →</a></article><article><h3>Product</h3><p>Current formula, product format, directions and authorization context.</p><a href="/pages/product-details">Product Details →</a></article><article><h3>Science</h3><p>Hydration mechanisms, formula rationale, publications and research status.</p><a href="/pages/research-publications">Research & Impact →</a></article><article><h3>Performance</h3><p>Athlete context, performance hydration education and current news coverage.</p><a href="/pages/performance-hydration">Performance Hydration →</a></article></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__feature"><div><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Citation-ready sources</p><h2>Link to the maintained page that supports the fact</h2><p>When a story references a specific Best Hydrate fact, journalists, partners and organizations can link directly to the maintained source page rather than a generic homepage. This keeps readers closer to the underlying context and makes future updates easier to verify.</p><ul><li><a href="/pages/publications"><strong>Peer-Reviewed Publications</strong></a> — authors, journal, DOI and current publication status.</li><li><a href="/pages/hydration-science"><strong>Hydration Science</strong></a> — physiology and oral-hydration education.</li><li><a href="/pages/our-formula"><strong>Our Formula</strong></a> — current ingredients and formulation rationale.</li><li><a href="/pages/research-partners"><strong>Research Partners</strong></a> — current collaboration context and affiliation boundaries.</li><li><a href="/pages/current-research"><strong>Current Research</strong></a> — active and planned research streams with status labels.</li><li><a href="/pages/dianna-proctor"><strong>Dianna Proctor</strong></a> — current Best Hydrate athlete-ambassador context.</li></ul><p>For the accepted Frontiers review, the publisher record and DOI remain the independent scholarly source; Best Hydrate's publication page provides current company context and status.</p></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__split"><div class="bhd-page__split-media"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/6953842/pexels-photo-6953842.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1500" alt="Two professionals discussing a business topic during an interview" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" fetchpriority="low"></div><div class="bhd-page__split-copy"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Interview topics</p><h2>Areas where Best Hydrate can provide company perspective</h2><ul><li>Hydration product development and ingredient rationale</li><li>Why glucose and electrolytes appear together in oral hydration science</li><li>Building a research program around an early-stage consumer brand</li><li>Performance hydration and athlete collaboration</li><li>Responsible boundaries between consumer hydration and clinical applications</li><li>Humanitarian access as an implementation and safe-water problem</li></ul><p>For technical scientific interviews, requests may be routed to the most appropriate available contributor rather than assuming every company spokesperson is an expert in every topic.</p></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid"><article class="bhd-page__prose"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">News archive</p><h2>Use dated articles for dated claims</h2><p>The News & Insights archive includes athlete results, sponsorship updates and hydration commentary. Because sport results, research status and company plans change, journalists should use the article date and confirm any current-status statement before publication.</p><p>Older blog posts may also contain language that predates the current science-first site rebuild. For current product and scientific positioning, the dedicated Science and Product pages take precedence.</p></article><aside class="bhd-page__callout"><span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Media standard</span><h3>Date-sensitive facts should be rechecked.</h3><p>Results, affiliations, research status and product information can change after an article is published.</p></aside></section>

